.TH UCABLE-AGENT-HELPER 1 "2026-10-28" "ucabled" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ucable\-agent\-helper \- QR code window for ucabled
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ucable\-agent\-helper
.RB [ \-\-rp " RP" ]
.RB [ \-\-layer\-shell ]
.RB [ \-\-also\-key ]
.RB [ \-\-timeout " SECS" ]
.RB [ \-\-request\-type " mc|ga" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The helper is spawned by
.BR ucable\-agent (1)
for a single prompt and exits when that interaction ends.
It is not usually run by hand; any UI can replace it as long as it follows
the contract in
.IR docs/helper-contract.md .
.PP
It reads the caBLE URL from the first line of standard input and renders it
as a QR code; a later
.B found
line blurs the code and asks the user to confirm on the phone.
.PP
Press Esc or close the window to give up on the prompt; there is no header
bar to close under
.BR \-\-layer\-shell ,
so Esc is the only way out on such a surface.
.PP
The URL is a per-transaction secret, so it only ever travels over standard
input.  Everything on the command line is display-only and world-readable
via /proc; unknown arguments, including any FIDO:/ URL, are ignored.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-rp " RP"
Show the relying party
.I RP
above the QR code.  Display-only.
.TP
.B \-\-layer\-shell
Draw as a Wayland layer\-shell surface instead of a window.
.TP
.B \-\-also\-key
Another authenticator is connected: note in the window that touching it
also answers the prompt.  The note disappears once the phone is detected.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SECS"
Replace the QR code with a "Code expired" page after
.I SECS
seconds, so a code that outlived its transaction is no longer on screen.
The window stays open until the user closes it.  Default 300;
0 disables the expiry.
.TP
.BI \-\-request\-type " mc|ga"
Phrase the caption for
.B mc
(authenticatorMakeCredential) or
.B ga
(authenticatorGetAssertion).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B UCABLED_HELPER_LAYER_SHELL
Truthy to imply
.BR \-\-layer\-shell .
.SH EXIT STATUS
The agent only observes that the process exited; it does not distinguish
exit codes.  The reference helper exits 0 after Esc, the window close button
or an expired code, and a non\-zero status means it failed to start rather
than that the user cancelled.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ucabled (1),
.BR ucable\-agent (1)
